<title>USA: Chancellor plans private offering.</title>
<headline>Chancellor plans private offering.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor Broadcasting Co said on Friday it and its Chancellor Radio Broadcasting Co unit were beginning a private securities offering to raise money to allow them to complete the purchase of 20 radio stations.</p>
<p>The company previously announced plans to buy eight radio stations from OmniAmerica Group and 12 radio stations from Colfax Communications.</p>
<p>Chancellor Broadcasting said it would offer $100 million liquidation preference of a new class of convertible preferred stock. Chancellor Radio would receive the net proceeds as equity, for use in the pending acquisitions, it said.</p>
<p>The convertible preferred stock would be convertible, at a price to be determined, into shares of Chancellor's class A common stock.</p>
<p>((--New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
